I agree. I used to be a Moria fun, and switched to NetHack about one and a
half months ago after I won that game 5 times. Casting spell is probably
the only thing NetHack doesn't handle well. I don't think NetHack need to
be like Moria that a spell caster must carry magic books, but I do think
that some spells should have unlimited uses, like detect monster, force bolt,
etc. Powerful spells like finger of death or genocide should still have
limited uses. Oh, extra healing as well, otherwise one can get infinite
hit points. The ability of casting spell (chace of success) should depend on 
intelligence, the cost of the spells should be increased, and the energy 
points should be decreased such that a high level character can still run 
out of energy keeping on casting spells. 

Wizards and Priests should be better than other characters in casting spells,
let's say, more eneries. Of course, wizards have another advantage, high 
intelligence. To balance that, their fighting ability should be reduced.
They should start with nothing but some spellbooks. (otherwise wizard is too
good to start as they have a bunch of magic goodies)

Spell casters should never be as good at fighting as pure fighters even
though they raise to the same strength and dexterity (as in the newiest 
version of Moria, I think that's a good move), meanwhile fighters should not
be as good at casting spells even they finally get the intelligence of
a wizard.

Well, these are just my opinions. The point is, spellbooks shouldn't be
wands that require intelligence to use.

It is funny to see that we are talking about increase the magic abilites of
spell casters, while in rec.games.moria, people are talking about how to
make a warrior competitable with other character for high level. 


